      "message": "Thanks for the contribution.\nSkParagraph is designed as a text layout engine for interactive UI rendering, and the text blobs created in `Run::copyTo` are an internal drawing cache for raster/GPU backends where text and cluster metadata are not needed. We cannot populate these blobs with UTF-8 source text.\nIf your use case requires extracting positioned glyphs alongside their original Unicode text and cluster indices (for example, to construct text blobs for PDF export), please use `Paragraph::visit` or `Paragraph::extendedVisit` instead, which are designed specifically for this purpose.",
